-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner involution preserves the ℤ₍ₚ₎[j]-chart of X₀(Np)
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid N$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * p)` for the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $Np$. Let $\mathcal{O}=$ `chartAlgFin (N * p) p` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$, that is over the subalgebra generated by the single element $j$ viewed in $F$; and let $w_p=$ `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull N p` be the chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ interchanging $j(q^{d})$ and $j(q^{dp})$ for every nonzero $d\mid N$ (the identity automorphism if no such automorphism exists). The assertion is that there is a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra automorphism $w$ of $\mathcal{O}$ such that for every $b\in\mathcal{O}$ the element $w(b)$, viewed in $F$, equals $w_p(b)$, and such that $w$ composed with itself is the identity automorphism of $\mathcal{O}$. In particular $w_p$ maps the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ in $F$ onto itself.
--
--   This is the statement that the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ of $X_0(Np)$, $p\nmid N$, preserves the affine chart of the integral model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ obtained as the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$, and induces an involution of its coordinate ring. It is used in the construction of the corresponding involution of the Igusa-type scheme glued from the finite and infinite charts, and downstream in the analysis of the fibre and of residue-field base changes of the chart algebra.
-- source:
